      "message": "This is used to back LinkAddress and IpPrefix; before this change, I think the following would work:\n\nnew IpPrefix(\"[2001:db8::123]/64\")\nnew IpPrefix(\"/64\")\n\nChanging behavior for the LinkAddress and IpPrefix system API might not be OK. Maybe you could have a @Deprecated legacyParseIpAndMask method that checks for empty strings (like in libcore/ojluni/src/main/java/java/net/InetAddress.java) and strips brackets (like InetAddressUtils.parseNumericAddressNoThrowStripOptionalBrackets) and have LinkAddress and IpPrefix use that ? Also add tests for parsing the legacy format in IpPrefix / LinkAddress.\n\nIdeally you would use http://go/nonsdk/dev/compat-framework to have the LinkAddress and IpPrefix methods use the new behavior on newer target SDK, but this is a bit scary on upgrade as apps / settings may have user-provided stored addresses as strings, so it\u0027s not easy for them to check they don\u0027t have the wrong format (maybe we should deprecated the constructors and have .parse methods instead...)",
